   3:Core/Src/termistor.c **** /**
   4:Core/Src/termistor.c ****  * @brief Converts the voltage from a voltage divider circuit to temperature in degrees Celsius.
   5:Core/Src/termistor.c ****  * 
   6:Core/Src/termistor.c ****  * This function uses the Steinhart-Hart equation to calculate the temperature of a thermistor
   7:Core/Src/termistor.c ****  * based on the voltage measured from a voltage divider circuit.
   8:Core/Src/termistor.c ****  * 
   9:Core/Src/termistor.c ****  * Be careful when choosing the KY-013 voltage level. If 5000.0 millivolts (5.0 V) is used, bear in
  10:Core/Src/termistor.c ****  * voltage on the STM32F411 ADC Pin must not exceed 3300.0 millivolts (3.3 V). Thus, the current fl
  11:Core/Src/termistor.c ****  * circuit should not exceed 330 uA. So, if the thermistor resistance becomes lower than 5151.52 oh
  12:Core/Src/termistor.c ****  * the ADC pin will be exceeded. For a 10 kohms NTC Thermistor, this represents a temperature highe
  13:Core/Src/termistor.c ****  * 
  14:Core/Src/termistor.c ****  * @param Pin1Voltage_mV The supply voltage of the KY-013 (Pin 1, which has a - sign), in millivolt
  15:Core/Src/termistor.c ****  * @param readVoltage_mV The voltage over the fixed resistor (divider_R) read on Pin 2, in millivol
  16:Core/Src/termistor.c ****  * 
  17:Core/Src/termistor.c ****  * @return The temperature in degrees Celsius.
  18:Core/Src/termistor.c ****  */
